---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/ui/Eyebrow.astro";

// Plain-language privacy notice. Keep it honest and specific: it should match
// what the site actually collects (contact form, audit tool, analytics) — if
// those change, update this page.
const updated = "July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Pixelboost handles the information you share: the contact form, the free website audit, and privacy-friendly analytics. Plain language, no surprises."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="section-card surface-paper privacy">
      <Eyebrow label="Privacy" />
      <h1 class="privacy-h1">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-lead">
        I'm Josh, and Pixelboost is a one-person web studio. This page explains what
        information this site collects, why, and what I do with it. No jargon, no
        surprises. If anything here isn't clear, just <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="privacy-body">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          I collect only what I need to reply to you and to run the free scan you
          asked for. I don't sell your information, I don't share it with advertisers,
          and I use privacy-friendly analytics that don't track you across the web or
          set advertising cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>What I collect, and when</h2>

        <h3>When you use the contact form</h3>
        <p>
          You choose what to send: typically your name, email, a message, and
          optionally your current website address. I use this only to reply to you
          and, if you shared a website, to take a quick look before I do. That's it.
        </p>

        <h3>When you run the free website audit</h3>
        <p>
          The audit tool takes the website address you enter and runs it through
          Google's PageSpeed Insights to score its speed, accessibility, SEO, and
          setup. Entering your own email is optional — if you do, I use it to send
          you the scan results and, sometimes, to follow up about your site. The URL
          you scan is also sent to me so I can see who's checking their site. If you
          don't want that, don't enter an email, but the scanned URL is still shared
          with me.
        </p>

        <h3>Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          I use a self-hosted copy of <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Plausible Analytics</a>
          to understand which pages get visited. Plausible is privacy-first: it uses
          no cookies, collects no personal data, and doesn't follow you around the
          internet. I see aggregate numbers (page views, rough locations, referrers),
          never anything that identifies you personally.
        </p>

        <h2>The tools that keep this site running</h2>
        <p>
          A few services process data on my behalf to make this site work and keep
          it secure:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts and delivers the site, and helps protect it from abuse.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> is a privacy-friendly CAPTCHA alternative that checks the contact form and audit tool aren't being abused by bots. It doesn't track you.</li>
          <li><strong>Google PageSpeed Insights</strong> is the engine behind the free audit; the URL you scan is sent to Google to be measured.</li>
          <li><strong>Fastmail</strong> is where the emails from the contact form and audit tool land, so I can read and reply to them.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How long I keep things</h2>
        <p>
          I keep contact and audit emails as long as I need them to help you or to
          keep a record of our conversation, and no longer than is reasonable. If you'd
          like me to delete what I have about you, just ask and I'll take care of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can email me any time to see what information I hold about you, to
          correct it, or to have it deleted. You're never on a mailing list you didn't
          ask to join — I don't run one.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about any of this? Email <a href="mailto:josh@pixelboost.ca">josh@pixelboost.ca</a>
          or use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: {updated}.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy { max-width: 820px; }
  .privacy-h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px); font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 12px 0 18px; line-height: 1.05;
  }
  .privacy-lead {
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.4vw, 19px); color: var(--color-ink-500);
    line-height: 1.6; max-width: 62ch; margin: 0 0 8px; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .privacy-body { margin-top: 28px; }
  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 26px); font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 36px 0 10px;
  }
  .privacy-body h3 {
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 19px); font-weight: 700;
    margin: 22px 0 6px; color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .privacy-body p, .privacy-body li {
    font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-700);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
  .privacy-body p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .privacy-body ul { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .privacy-body a {
    color: var(--color-mint-700); text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .privacy-body a:hover { color: var(--color-mint-600); }
  .privacy-updated {
    margin-top: 32px; font-size: 13px; font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
</style>
